  "step_3": "The information considered by the individual (outcome magnitude and probability comparison) does not include the aspiration level (mean of outcomes) or any evaluation of positive differences from that level. The individual does not reference a benchmark or mean value. Their justification is based on the higher prize in Lottery B and a subjective assessment of the probability difference as negligible. The decision reason, however, requires evaluating which lottery has a higher probability of yielding an outcome above the mean (aspiration level). In this case, Lottery A has a higher probability (25% vs. 20%) of exceeding the aspiration level, so the reason would favor A. The individual chose B, which contradicts the reason’s recommendation. More importantly, the reasoning process described does not involve the aspiration level or the evaluation of positive differences. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation. The individual’s justification is inconsistent with the reason’s rule and does not reflect its application.",
